Supreme People's Court

Interim Regulations on Judicial Police of the People's Courts

Fa Fa [1997] No. 11

Chapter I General Provisions

Article 1 These Regulations are formulated in accordance with the Organic Law of the People's Courts of the People's Republic of China and the People's Police Law of the People's Republic of China for the purposes of strengthening the construction of the judicial police force of the people's courts, achieving scientific management of judicial police, improving the quality of judicial police, and ensuring that judicial police exercise their functions and powers according to law.

Article 2 Judicial police of the people's courts are one of the branches of the People's Police of the People's Republic of China.

Article 3 The task of judicial police of the people's courts is, through the exercise of their functions and powers, to prevent, stop, and punish illegal and criminal acts that obstruct trial activities, maintain trial order, and ensure the smooth conduct of trial work.

Article 4 The Supreme People's Court directs the judicial police work of local people's courts at various levels and special people's courts, and a higher people's court directs the judicial police work of lower people's courts.

Article 5 Judicial police of the people's courts must take the Constitution and laws as the norms for their conduct, serve the people wholeheartedly, be loyal to their duties, be honest and upright, obey orders, and strictly enforce the law.

Article 6 Judicial police of the people's courts performing their duties according to law shall be protected by law.

Chapter II Functions and Powers

Article 7 The duties of judicial police of the people's courts are:
(1) Guarding the court and maintaining trial order;
(2) When on duty in court, being responsible for summoning witnesses and expert evaluators and transmitting evidentiary materials;
(3) Serving legal documents;
(4) Executing summons, compulsory summons, and detention;
(5) Escorting, transporting, and guarding defendants or criminals;
(6) Participating in the sealing up, seizure, freezing, or confiscation of property pursuant to judgments or rulings;
(7) Executing the death penalty;
(8) Other duties as prescribed by laws and regulations.

Article 8 Judicial police of the people's courts perform their duties under the direction of judges.

Article 9 Judicial police of the people's courts may, when performing their duties, take coercive measures according to law; they may use police instruments according to relevant state regulations as needed; if the use of police instruments cannot stop the conduct or the use of weapons is necessary to prevent serious harmful consequences, they may use weapons according to relevant state regulations.

Article 10 To ensure the safety of trial premises, judicial police of the people's courts may conduct security checks on persons entering the trial premises who are not performing duties according to law; they shall take measures according to law against persons who are unsuitable to enter the trial premises or who are suspected of illegal or criminal activities.

Article 11 To maintain court order, judicial police of the people's courts shall, in accordance with the instructions of the presiding judge or the sole adjudicator, take coercive measures against persons who violate court rules.

Chapter III Organization and Management

Article 12 The establishment and organizational structure of judicial police of the people's courts shall be prescribed by the Supreme People's Court.

Article 13 Judicial police of the people's courts shall be managed in organizational units. The Supreme People's Court shall establish a Judicial Police Bureau, higher people's courts shall establish Judicial Police Corps, intermediate people's courts shall establish Judicial Police Sub-Corps, and basic people's courts shall establish Judicial Police Detachments.

Article 14 Judicial police of the people's courts are subject to the leadership of the president of the people's court to which they belong and accept the management of that people's court and the judicial police department of the higher people's court.

Article 15 The main duties of the Judicial Police Bureau of the Supreme People's Court are:
(1) Studying and drafting regulations, provisions, and measures concerning judicial police work;
(2) Studying and formulating plans and measures for the construction of the judicial police force;
(3) Directing and supervising the professional work of judicial police of local people's courts at various levels;
(4) Inspecting and supervising the implementation of laws and regulations by judicial police;
(5) Directing the work of reporting and approving police ranks of local people's courts at various levels;
(6) Managing the police ranks of judicial police at the rank of Police Supervisor and above;
(7) Organizing education and training for judicial police;
(8) Coordinating major police activities across provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government;
(9) Managing the equipment of judicial police;
(10) Completing other tasks assigned by the President.

Article 16 The main duties of the Judicial Police Corps of a higher people's court are:
(1) Organizing the implementation of regulations, provisions, and measures concerning judicial police work;
(2) Studying, drafting, organizing, and implementing rules and detailed regulations for judicial police management;
(3) Directing and supervising the professional work of judicial police of lower people's courts;
(4) Inspecting and supervising the implementation of laws and regulations by judicial police;
(5) Managing the police ranks of judicial police at the rank of Police Superintendent and below;
(6) Organizing education and training for judicial police;
(7) Coordinating major police activities across regions within its jurisdiction;
(8) Managing the equipment of judicial police;
(9) Completing other tasks assigned by the President.

Article 17 The main duties of the Judicial Police Sub-Corps of an intermediate people's court are:
(1) Organizing the implementation of regulations, provisions, and measures concerning judicial police work;
(2) Organizing the implementation of rules and detailed regulations for judicial police management;
(3) Formulating and implementing work plans for judicial police;
(4) Organizing judicial police to perform their duties;
(5) Directing police work within its jurisdiction;
(6) Organizing education and training for judicial police;
(7) Managing the equipment of judicial police;
(8) Completing other tasks assigned by the President.

Article 18 The main duties of the Judicial Police Detachment of a basic people's court are:
(1) Organizing the implementation of regulations, provisions, and measures concerning judicial police work;
(2) Organizing the implementation of rules and detailed regulations for judicial police management;
(3) Formulating and implementing work plans for judicial police;
(4) Organizing judicial police to perform their duties;
(5) Organizing education and training for judicial police;
(6) Managing the equipment of judicial police;
(7) Completing other tasks assigned by the President.

Article 19 To serve as judicial police of a people's court, the following conditions must be met:
(1) Being a citizen who has reached the age of eighteen;
(2) Upholding the Constitution of the People's Republic of China;
(3) Having good political and professional qualities and good conduct;
(4) Being in good health;
(5) Having an educational level of senior high school graduation or above;
(6) Voluntarily engaging in judicial police work.

No person shall serve as judicial police under any of the following circumstances:
(1) Having previously received criminal punishment;
(2) Having previously been discharged from public employment;
(3) Having previously been dismissed by a state organ.

Article 20 When recruiting judicial police, people's courts must, in accordance with state regulations, conduct open examinations, strict assessment, and select the best candidates for employment.

Newly recruited judicial police shall have a probation period of one year. Those who pass the assessment upon expiration of the probation period shall be formally appointed and have their corresponding police rank evaluated and conferred; those who fail shall have their employment qualification revoked.

Article 21 The classification of ranks and grades of judicial police of the people's courts shall be implemented by reference to the relevant provisions of the Interim Regulations on State Civil Servants.

Judicial police of the people's courts shall implement the police rank system according to law.

Article 22 When transferring judicial police, the people's court shall solicit the opinions of its judicial police department; the appointment and removal of the principal responsible person of the judicial police department shall be reported to the judicial police department of the higher people's court for recordation.

Article 23 Based on the nature, tasks, and characteristics of judicial police of the people's courts, the maximum ages for transferring persons from other departments to serve as judicial police at different levels are: for clerical staff and section members, not exceeding twenty-five years of age; for section level, not exceeding thirty-five years of age; for deputy division level, not exceeding forty-five years of age.

Article 24 Judicial police of the people's courts must wear uniforms as prescribed, display police rank insignia, armbands, and police badge numbers, maintain a neat appearance, and behave with dignity.

When performing duties, judicial police of the people's courts must carry their police officer identification cards.

Article 25 Rewards and punishments for judicial police of the people's courts shall be handled in accordance with the People's Police Law of the People's Republic of China and the relevant provisions of the Supreme People's Court.

Chapter IV Police Service Guarantees

Article 26 The police insignia, uniforms, and police instruments of judicial police of the people's courts shall be uniformly supervised by the Ministry of Public Security, and the Supreme People's Court shall manage them jointly with the Ministry of Public Security; no other individuals or organizations may illegally manufacture or sell them.

The police rank insignia, armbands, police badge numbers, police officer identification cards, uniforms, and police instruments of judicial police of the people's courts are for the exclusive use of judicial police; no other individuals or organizations may possess or use them.

Article 27 The funds required for the work and training of judicial police of the people's courts shall be guaranteed and included in the financial budget of the court.

Article 28 People's courts shall strengthen the modernization of judicial police equipment and plan to improve the transportation, communication, and other equipment and facilities necessary for judicial police work.

Article 29 Judicial police of the people's courts shall implement the state civil servant salary system and shall enjoy the police rank allowances, other allowances and subsidies, and insurance welfare benefits prescribed by the state.

Chapter V Supplementary Provisions

Article 30 These Regulations shall be interpreted by the Supreme People's Court.

Article 31 These Regulations shall come into force as of the date of promulgation.

May 4, 1997
